-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Exemption of Broadcasting Services by Educational Institutions) Order 2010 (S 523/2010), made under s 60 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-exemption-educational-institutions-order-2010/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S523-2010.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- THE SCHEDULE (which services are "exempt broadcasting services", para 2) IS NOT IN THE TEXT SERVED: whether a given service is an exempt broadcasting service is asked as a fact.

§ `Paragraph 2: Definitions`

-- src:7 | “educational institution” means an organisation for the provision of education;
@ref para 2 "educational institution" (src:7)
GIVEN `it is an organisation for the provision of education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 523/2010 para 2 the organisation is an educational institution` MEANS
    `it is an organisation for the provision of education`

-- src:8 | “exempt broadcasting service” means a licensable broadcasting service specified in the Schedule.
@ref para 2 "exempt broadcasting service" (src:8)
-- The Schedule is not in the text served; the answer is the fact asked.
GIVEN `it is a licensable broadcasting service specified in the Schedule to the Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 523/2010 para 2 the service is an exempt broadcasting service` MEANS
    `it is a licensable broadcasting service specified in the Schedule to the Order`

§ `Paragraphs 3 and 4: Exemption and its conditions`

-- src:10 | 3. Every educational institution shall be exempt from section 8 of the Act in relation to all or any exempt broadcasting service provided by that educational institution, subject to the terms and conditions specified in paragraph 4.
-- src:12 | 4. The exemption of an educational institution under paragraph 3 in relation to any exempt broadcasting service it provides or is to provide shall be subject to the following terms and conditions:
-- src:13 | ( a ) the educational institution shall inform the Authority —
-- src:14 | (i) where the educational institution is providing the exempt broadcasting service immediately before 16th September 2010, within one month from that date; or
-- src:15 | (ii) in any other case, no later than one month before the launch of the exempt broadcasting service;
-- src:16 | ( b ) the educational institution shall provide the exempt broadcasting service for the primary purpose of training its students or any class thereof;
-- src:17 | ( c ) the educational institution shall take reasonable steps to ensure —
-- src:18 | (i) that any special interest television service or special interest radio service transmitted through the educational institution’s closed Internet protocol network is received or capable of reception only by the educational institution’s officers, employees, consultants, agents or students; and
-- src:19 | (ii) that the exempt broadcasting service is otherwise not capable of reception by any person outside the premises of the educational institution;
-- src:20 | ( d ) the educational institution, in providing the exempt broadcasting service —
-- src:21 | (i) shall ensure that the exempt broadcasting service is not used for, or in furtherance of, any gaming or public lottery the conduct of which is an offence under the Common Gaming Houses Act (Cap. 49);
-- src:22 | (ii) shall not broadcast horse-racing analyses, commentaries or tips, or horse-racing results;
-- src:23 | (iii) shall ensure that the exempt broadcasting service is not used to advertise, offer services relating to or otherwise promote —
-- src:24 | (A) astrology;
-- src:25 | (B) geomancy;
-- src:26 | (C) palmistry; or
-- src:27 | (D) any other type of fortune-telling device;
-- src:28 | (iv) shall ensure, in the case of the exhibition of films (within the meaning of the Films Act (Cap. 107)) on the exempt broadcasting service, that only films that are approved by the Board of Film Censors for exhibition under that Act or that are exempt under section 40 of that Act are so exhibited; and
-- src:29 | (v) shall ensure that the exempt broadcasting service is not used for any purpose, and does not contain any programme, that is against the public interest, public order or national harmony or that offends good taste or decency.
@ref paras 3 and 4 (src:10-29)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person is an educational institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is an exempt broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it informed the Authority as paragraph 4(a) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides the service for the primary purpose of training its students or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it takes reasonable steps to ensure that a special interest television or radio service on its closed Internet protocol network is received or capable of reception only by its officers, employees, consultants, agents or students, and that the service is otherwise not capable of reception outside its premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it ensures the service is not used for gaming or public lottery that is an offence under the Common Gaming Houses Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does not broadcast horse-racing analyses, commentaries or tips, or results` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it ensures the service is not used to advertise, offer services relating to or promote astrology, geomancy, palmistry or another fortune-telling device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it ensures that, for films exhibited, only films approved by the Board of Film Censors or exempt under section 40 of the Films Act are exhibited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it ensures the service is not used for a purpose, and contains no programme, against the public interest, public order or national harmony or offending good taste or decency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 523/2010 paras 3 and 4 the institution is exempt from section 8 of the Act in relation to the service, on` MEANS
    IF `the Educational Institutions Exemption Order as deposited is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (`the person is an educational institution` AND `the service is an exempt broadcasting service`
        AND `it informed the Authority as paragraph 4(a) requires`
        AND `it provides the service for the primary purpose of training its students or any class of them`
        AND `it takes reasonable steps to ensure that a special interest television or radio service on its closed Internet protocol network is received or capable of reception only by its officers, employees, consultants, agents or students, and that the service is otherwise not capable of reception outside its premises`
        AND `it ensures the service is not used for gaming or public lottery that is an offence under the Common Gaming Houses Act`
        AND `it does not broadcast horse-racing analyses, commentaries or tips, or results`
        AND `it ensures the service is not used to advertise, offer services relating to or promote astrology, geomancy, palmistry or another fortune-telling device`
        AND `it ensures that, for films exhibited, only films approved by the Board of Film Censors or exempt under section 40 of the Films Act are exhibited`
        AND `it ensures the service is not used for a purpose, and contains no programme, against the public interest, public order or national harmony or offending good taste or decency`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:31 | 5. Nothing in this Order shall be construed to limit or in any way affect the operation of any other written law.
@ref para 5 (src:31)
GIVEN `another written law applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 523/2010 para 5 the Order limits or affects the operation of the other written law` MEANS
    IF `another written law applies` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
